  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project to Facilitate and Assist the Return of Displaced Persons Exposed to Protection Risks in Kaga Bandoro and Bria, Central African Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the presence of voluntary return intentions and threats of evictions at sites in the towns of Bria and Kaga Bandoro in the Central African Republic, this project intends to assist these internally displaced persons (IDPs) by providing them with a minimum return support package in this first emergency phase. Based on its extensive experience in supporting returns in Bangassou and Bambari, IOM is providing Camp Coordination and Camp Management and Shelter/Non-Food Item support over a period of six months to assist 11,000 people in Kaga Bandoro and Bria.</narrative>
  </description>
